      en: "Fuerte Santa Bárbara in Santo Domingo is a 16th-century fortress that defended the city from attacks. It sits on a hill offering wide views of the harbor. The fort is dedicated to Saint Barbara. It consists of stone walls and a chapel. Today it is a popular attraction. The site was restored in 1975 and houses a historical museum.",
