      en: "The Memorial Museum of the Resistance in Santo Domingo was established in 2010 on the site of a former torture center used by Trujillo's regime. The museum documents the resistance movement from 1930 to 1961 through interactive exhibits, photographs, and personal effects. It features reconstructed prison cells and a timeline of key events. The museum aims to promote human rights and democracy. It receives 40,000 visitors annually. Entry is free to survivors and their families.",
