      en: "Puerta de la Misericordia (Mercy Gate) in Santo Domingo is a 16th-century city gate built in 1542. It is made of coral stone with a semicircular arch. It was one of the main entrances to the walled city. During the 19th century, it was used as a prison and execution site. It was declared a National Monument in 1979. The gate is located at the northern end of Calle El Conde. It now serves as a cultural landmark.",
